<title>AUSTRIA: Over 80 injured in Austrian train crash.</title>
<headline>Over 80 injured in Austrian train crash.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Over 80 people were injured, including many children, when two regional trains collided on Tuesday in the region of Arbing in Upper Austria, state television reported.</p>
<p>In all 88 people were hurt in the crash, 10 seriously. Many of the casualties were children returning from school outings.</p>
<p>Some of the injured were flown to hospital by emergency helicopter, the television said.</p>
<p>The accident happened when one of the train drivers failed to heed a stop signal, it noted.</p>
</text>
